#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# dedekind_eta

#% text
# `dedekind_eta(tau)` gives the Dedekind eta function `eta(tau)`, for `im_part(tau) > 0`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `eta(tau)` is `exp(pi*im*tau/12)` times the product of `1 - exp(2*pi*im*k*tau)` over `k >= 1` (DLMF 27.14.12); it satisfies `eta(-1/tau) = sqrt(-im*tau)*eta(tau)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
dedekind_eta(1.0*im)
#% output
#= 0.7682254223260567 + 0.0im

#% cell
dedekind_eta(0.5 + 1.0*im)
#% output
#= 0.7645031667971424 + 0.10064875132231726im

#% cell
dedekind_eta(2.0*im)
#% output
#= 0.592382781332416 + 0.0im

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The product formula, with `q = exp(-2*pi)`:

#% cell
dedekind_eta(1.0*im) - exp(-pi/12.0)*q_pochhammer(exp(-2*pi*1.0))
#% output
#= 0.0 + 0.0im

#% text
# The transformation under `tau -> -1/tau`:

#% cell
dedekind_eta(-1/(0.2 + 1.5*im)) - sqrt(-im*(0.2 + 1.5*im))*dedekind_eta(0.2 + 1.5*im)
#% output
#= 1.1102230246251565e-16 - 2.2898349882893854e-16im

#% section
# See also

#% text
